---
title: Reconciliation
description: Turn your bank movements into bookings, invoice payments included.
---

Reconciling means telling nullish what each bank movement is: a client paying an invoice, rent, a software subscription, and so on. Each one you reconcile is booked in your journal.

Open a bank account and choose **Reconcile**. You see every movement that's still **To reconcile**.

## Payments matched with an invoice

When a client pays a QR-bill, the payment carries the invoice's reference. nullish recognizes it and suggests the invoice under **Matched with an invoice**.

- Choose **Book payment** to record the payment. The invoice becomes paid.
- If the amount doesn't cover the whole invoice, it stays open with what **Remains due**. Book the next payment the same way when it arrives.
- If the client paid too much, nullish shows it as **Overpaid** and books the difference.
- Wrong match? Choose **Not this invoice** and book the movement on an account instead.

## Movements to book on an account

Everything else is listed under **To book on an account**:

1. Pick the **Account**, e.g. `6570 IT costs` for a subscription.
2. Adjust the **Description** if you like. It's prefilled with the movement's communication.
3. Pick a **VAT rate** if VAT applies.
4. Choose **Book**.

## Ignore a movement

Some movements don't need a booking. Choose **Ignore** to set them aside.

{% aside type="caution" %}
An ignored movement books nothing and can't be reconciled afterwards. There's no undo, so ignore
with care.
{% /aside %}

## Good to know

- Only movements in your organization's currency can be reconciled for now.
- A reconciled movement can't be reconciled again. Double-check before booking.
- Once nothing is left, you'll see **Nothing to reconcile.**
